## Appendix: Why Only the Responses API? (Responses vs Chat Completions)

### Background — API Consolidation

The Responses API (launched early 2025) is OpenAI's deliberate consolidation of three APIs
into one:

    Chat Completions (stateless chat)  ──┐
    Assistants API (stateful agents)   ──┼──→  Responses API (unified)
    Legacy Completions                 ──┘

It is not an alternative to Chat Completions — it is its successor.

### Capability Comparison

| Capability                     | Chat Completions     | Responses API          |
|--------------------------------|----------------------|------------------------|
| Stateless prompt → response    | ✅                   | ✅                     |
| Server-side state              | ❌                   | ✅ (previous_response_id, store: true) |
| Built-in tools (web, code, file search) | ❌          | ✅ Native              |
| Multimodal (text + images)     | Limited              | ✅ Native              |
| Structured output (JSON schema)| Partial              | ✅ Native              |
| Cache utilization              | Moderate             | ~80% better (OpenAI benchmarks) |
| New model support (GPT-5+)    | Legacy only          | ✅ Primary             |

For a simple "send prompt, get text" use case, both work identically. But agents inherently
need tool use, state, and richer interaction — all Responses-native features that do not exist
in Chat Completions.

### Why the Application Endpoint Only Exposes Responses

This is intentional, not a gap. Microsoft chose the forward-looking protocol for their newest
endpoint type. Agent Applications need tools, structured outputs, and eventually stateful
conversations — all Responses-native features. Adding Chat Completions support would mean
exposing a legacy protocol on a new resource type designed for the future.

### Deprecation Timeline

| Event                                    | Date/Status          |
|------------------------------------------|----------------------|
| Responses API launched                   | Early 2025 — active, primary |
| Chat Completions                         | Now — legacy, supported but no new features |
| Chat Completions removed (OpenAI Codex)  | Feb 2026 — done      |
| Assistants API sunset                    | Aug 26, 2026         |
| Chat Completions general sunset          | TBD — no hard date, strongly discouraged for new projects |

### Implications for Our Decision

- Chat Completions is not coming to the application endpoint — Microsoft is moving forward.
- Options C (Azure.AI.Inference) and D (Microsoft.Extensions.AI / IChatClient) are built on
  Chat Completions, which further confirms they are not just technically incompatible today but
  are architecturally misaligned with where the platform is heading.
- Our choice of the OpenAI SDK with `ResponsesClient` (Option B) is aligned with both
  OpenAI's and Microsoft's strategic direction.
- The Responses API will be where all future investment goes — new models, new tools, new
  features, and eventually the restoration of server-managed conversations on the application
  endpoint.

